.TH KSPKAN 1 2026-11-25 "kspkan 0.5.0"
.SH NAME
kspkan \- small mod manager for Kerbal Space Program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kspkan
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command " [" args ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kspkan
installs, removes and upgrades Kerbal Space Program mods using the
CKAN module list (CKAN-meta).  It resolves dependencies (depends,
any_of, provides, conflicts), offers recommended and suggested mods,
checks every download against its SHA-256 or SHA-1 sum, and records
each file it installs, so that removal deletes exactly those files.
.PP
With no command it opens a full screen mode; press
.B ?
there for the keys.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI update " [file]"
Fetch the module list.  With a
.IR file ,
read a CKAN-meta .tar.gz fetched some other way (over Tor, on another
computer) instead of downloading.
.TP
.BI search " [query]"
List modules.  Words are ANDed; a leading \- excludes a word.  Also:
.IR author:x " " tag:x " " license:x " " needs:x " " dl>5k " " dl<100
.IR after:2024-01-01 " " before:... " " size<5 " (MB) "
.IR is:installed " " is:chosen " " is:dep " " is:needed " " is:orphan
.IR is:update " " is:new " and "
.IR sort:pop | new | small | big | name .
.TP
.BI show " id"
Describe a module.
.TP
.B list
Installed modules: those you chose, then the dependencies, each with
the modules that need it.  A dependency nothing needs is pointed out
(autoremove takes it).  Modules found in the game are marked (found);
then the DLCs and the GameData directories the module list does not
know.
.TP
.BI compat " [version ... | none]"
Other game versions whose modules count as fitting this game too, as
CKAN's compatible game versions; 1.12 stands for every 1.12.x.  Kept
for each game; with no version, shows them.
.TP
.B scan
Find the mods already in the game, put there by CKAN (from
CKAN/registry.json) or by hand (matched by the directories and files
their metadata would make; the version from a file name or a .version
file, else ?), and mark them found.  This also happens on its own when
GameData or CKAN/registry.json has changed.  Found mods can be
upgraded and removed; their files are never moved.  DLCs and unknown
directories are only named.
.TP
.BI install " id[=version] ..."
Install modules and what they need.  Recommended and suggested modules
are offered for choosing.  When a dependency can come from several
modules (as Kerbalism-Config), the one named on the command line or in
the modlist is taken; otherwise kspkan asks which on the terminal.
.TP
.BI remove " id ..."
Remove modules, the modules that need them, and dependencies nothing
needs any more.
.TP
.BI upgrade " [id ...]"
Upgrade installed modules (all of them when none is named).
.TP
.B autoremove
Remove dependencies nothing needs.
.TP
.BI keep " id ..."
Mark installed modules as chosen by you, so that autoremove and the
removal of what needed them leave them in.  Installing a module that is
in as a dependency does the same.
.TP
.BI auto " id ..."
Mark installed modules as dependencies: autoremove takes them when
nothing needs them.
.TP
.BR modlist " [" list ]
The saved modlists.  A modlist is a plain text file with one
.RI \(dq id " " version \(dq
line for each module you chose (lines starting with # are comments);
the dependencies are worked out again when it is installed.
.TP
.BI "modlist save" " name"
Save the modules you chose as a modlist.
.TP
.BI "modlist show" " name"
What the modlist has, and how this game differs from it.
.TP
.BI "modlist install" " name"
Install what the modlist has and the game has not, at the newest
version that fits the game.
.TP
.BI "modlist pin" " name"
The same, at the very versions the modlist names.
.TP
.BI "modlist sync" " name"
Install the modlist, and remove the modules you chose that are not in
it.
.TP
.BI "modlist delete" " name"
Delete a modlist.  A
.I name
that is not a saved modlist is taken as a file, in the current directory
or anywhere, for example one somebody gave you.  A file CKAN wrote (see
.BR "modlist import" )
is first kept as a modlist named after it.
.TP
.BI "modlist import" " file [name]"
Read a list that CKAN wrote and keep it as a modlist called
.IR name ,
or after the file name without its extension.  It reads a .ckan
modpack (its depends and recommends; the first choice of any_of;
suggests is left out), CKAN/registry.json from a game folder (the mods
CKAN did not install as dependencies), a mod list CKAN saved as plain
text, Markdown, BBCode, CSV or TSV, and the output of
.BR "ckan list" .
CKAN's formats are only read, never written.
.TP
.B clean
Delete downloaded archives.
.TP
.BI add " name [gamedir]"
Remember a game folder (the folder that holds GameData) as an instance.
.TP
.BR instances ", " use " \fIname\fR, " forget " \fIname\fR"
List, choose or forget instances.  Forgetting never touches the game.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH FULL SCREEN MODE
The list marks each installed module
.B i
(chosen by you) or
.B d
(a dependency), and
.B u
when a newer version fits.
.B i
and
.B I
go through what is shown: all, installed, chosen by you,
dependencies, unneeded dependencies, not installed, updates, marked.
.B p
puts the description at the bottom, on the right (with everything
about the module: what needs it, the long description, links;
.BR J " and " K
scroll it), or turns it off; the choice is remembered.
.B e
makes an installed module your choice or a dependency.
.B w
saves the modules you chose as a modlist;
.B o
opens one and marks what the game lacks of it, ready for Enter.
.B O
imports a file CKAN wrote (see
.BR "modlist import" )
and opens it the same way.
.B ?
shows every key.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " name"
Use that instance (default: the last one used).
.TP
.BI \-g " dir"
Use that game folder directly.
.TP
.BI \-k " version"
The game version, when it cannot be read from the game folder.
.TP
.B \-a
Ignore game version compatibility.
.TP
.B \-t
Allow testing and development releases.
.TP
.B \-f
Overwrite files that kspkan did not install.
.TP
.B \-y
Do not ask for confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-S
Also install recommended (\-R), or recommended and suggested (\-S)
modules, without asking.
.TP
.B \-p
List the most downloaded first.
.TP
.B \-m
No colours on the screen.
.TP
.BI \-r " url"
Another module list archive.
.TP
.BI \-s " dir"
Keep all of kspkan's files in dir (used by the tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/kspkan
(or
.IR ~/.local/share/kspkan )
.BR instances :
the remembered game folders;
.BR index ", " summary ", " provides ", " counts ", " meta/ :
the module list;
.BR cache/ :
downloads;
.BR modlists/ :
the saved modlists;
.BR settings :
where the full screen mode puts the description;
.BI inst/ name /installed :
what was installed into each instance.  All are plain text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, the screen has no colours.
.TP
.BR ALL_PROXY ", " HTTPS_PROXY
Passed on to curl, which does the downloading.
.SH NOTES
Downloads are done by running
.BR curl (1).
Nothing else is contacted, and kspkan sends nothing about you or your
game anywhere.
